# Store every text file with LF and check it out with LF on every platform, so the bytes on
# disk match the bytes in the repository and nothing converts in either direction. The
# alternative — plain `text=auto`, which checks out CRLF on Windows — is what Roslyn and
# dotnet/runtime do, but it contradicts end_of_line = lf in .editorconfig. xunit, Humanizer,
# ReactiveUI, ImageSharp and MudBlazor all pin LF the same way.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Hunk headers name the enclosing type or member instead of showing a bare line range.
*.cs text diff=csharp

# Redundant while the rule above is eol=lf, but these must never be CRLF: the Rust parity
# fixture copies them into a Linux container, where a CR before a line continuation breaks
# the build. Stated explicitly so they survive a change to the default.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# BCS vectors are byte-exact wire fixtures. None are committed today — the Rust fixture
# generates them at test time — but EOL conversion would silently corrupt one that ever is.
*.bcs binary
